const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"怎样区分事件与市场本身？",en:"Separating an event from the market"},body:{zh:"MacKinlay介绍事件研究如何利用事件附近的证券价格考察经济影响。关键不是只看涨跌，而是先构造“没有这个事件时”的正常收益基准，再观察实际收益与基准的差异。",en:"MacKinlay reviews how security prices around an event can help study economic effects. The key is not the price move alone: define a normal-return benchmark without conditioning on the event, then compare actual performance with that benchmark."}},{title:{zh:"先定义意外消息，而不是先按涨跌分组",en:"Define the news surprise before grouping by returns"},body:{zh:"原文用季度盈余公告举例，研究对象是1989—1993年道指30家公司的公告，并依据实际盈余与预期的差异区分消息。编辑建议：事件分类要来自事先定义的信息，不能看到股价上涨后再把公告标为好消息，否则分类本身已包含了要解释的结果。",en:"The illustrative study concerns quarterly earnings announcements for 30 Dow firms in 1989–1993, classifying news by actual earnings relative to expectations. Editorial application: define event categories from a prespecified information measure, not the observed price response. Labeling rising-price events as good news embeds the outcome in the classification."},reference:{url:"https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txsd.1759270/gov.uscourts.txsd.1759270.250.1.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第3节：盈余公告示例",en:"Original §3: earnings-announcement example"}}},{title:{zh:"事件窗口与估计窗口分开",en:"Separate event and estimation windows"},body:{zh:"先定义事件和样本筛选条件，再确定事件窗口；正常收益模型通常用事件发生前、且不与事件窗口重叠的资料估计。盘后公告的影响可能进入次日，预先泄露或预期也可能体现在事件前，窗口选择因此属于研究设计的一部分。",en:"Define the event and sample selection before choosing its window. Normal-return models are commonly estimated on earlier, non-overlapping observations. After-hours announcements may affect the next session, while anticipation may appear earlier. Window selection is part of the design."}},{title:{zh:"异常收益只是分析的起点",en:"Abnormal returns are a starting point"},body:{zh:"计算异常收益后，还需要决定如何跨时间、跨公司汇总，以及如何进行统计推断。作者提醒样本偏差和少数观测的影响。某一天偏离市场，并不能单独证明事件造成了该变化。",en:"After computing abnormal returns, researchers must decide how to aggregate across time and firms and how to conduct inference. The review highlights selection bias and influential observations. A one-day departure from market performance alone does not prove causation."}},{title:{zh:"经济模型也需要统计假设",en:"Economic models still require statistical assumptions"},body:{zh:"第4节把正常收益模型区分为统计型与经济型：前者主要依赖收益过程假设，后者加入经济行为限制，但实际使用仍需要统计设定。选择更复杂的模型不是自动获得更强识别；应说明基准、估计期和残差性质为何适合这一类事件。",en:"Section 4 distinguishes statistical normal-return models from models imposing economic restrictions. Economic models still need statistical assumptions in practice. Complexity is not automatic identification strength: explain why the benchmark, estimation window and residual assumptions are appropriate for the event class being studied."},reference:{url:"https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txsd.1759270/gov.uscourts.txsd.1759270.250.1.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第4节：正常收益模型",en:"Original §4: models of normal performance"}}},{title:{zh:"从事件时间线开始准备",en:"Begin with an event timeline"},body:{zh:"本站建议先完成带时区的发布时间、首次可见时间、修订关系和交易日映射，再考虑收益计算。没有这些时点，精细的统计检验也无法修复错位的样本。教程中的时间线示例只完成这一步，不自动输出事件研究结论。",en:"Prepare timezone-aware release times, first-seen times, revisions and session mapping before computing returns. Statistical sophistication cannot repair a misaligned sample. The accompanying timeline tutorial completes this preparation step without producing an event-study conclusion."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"并发事件、样本选择和跨公司相关性会影响解释与推断。事件窗口中的相关性不自动构成因果识别。",en:"Confounding events, selection and cross-firm dependence affect interpretation and inference. Correlation within an event window is not automatic causal identification."}};export{e as default};
